@* Stands between the shell and a business screen, for an account that belongs to
   the platform rather than to a customer.

   Hiding the navigation is not enough on its own: an admin can still type
   /members, and a bookmark from a previous visit will. The screen behind it
   would query the ambient tenant — 0 — and come back with nothing, which reads
   as "this customer has no members" rather than "this is not yours to read".
   An empty state that lies about why it is empty is worse than no screen.

   What it says changed when the impersonation was removed. It used to invite the
   admin to enter a customer, because there was a door; now there is none, and
   promising one would be the same lie in the other direction. The screen states
   the boundary instead, and sends them back to the console — which is the whole
   of what their account opens.

   Administration is the exception it exists for: it is about the platform, not
   about a customer. *@

@inject NavigationManager Navigation

@if (Allowed)
{
    @ChildContent
}
else
{
    <div class="gx-empty">
        <GxIcon Name="@GxIconPaths.Shield" Size="28"/>
        <h3>Cet écran appartient à un client</h3>
        <p>
            Votre compte appartient à la plateforme. Les fiches membres, les plannings
            et les paiements restent dans l'espace du client — la console n'y donne pas
            accès. Pour dépanner quelqu'un, appelez-le ou demandez un partage d'écran.
        </p>
        <a class="gx-btn primary" href="@GxNavigation.Administration.Href">
            <GxIcon Name="@GxNavigation.Administration.Icon" Size="16"/>
            <span>Ouvrir la console</span>
        </a>
    </div>
}

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public TenantBrandDto Brand { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    private bool Allowed => !ConsoleBrand.IsConsole(Brand) || IsPlatformRoute;

    /// <summary>
    /// Matched on the path rather than on a flag the page sets, so a business
    /// screen cannot opt itself in by forgetting to.
    /// </summary>
    private bool IsPlatformRoute
    {
        get
        {
            var path = "/" + Navigation.ToBaseRelativePath(Navigation.Uri);
            var end = path.IndexOfAny(['?', '#']);
            if (end >= 0)
            {
                path = path[..end];
            }

            return path.StartsWith(GxNavigation.Administration.Href, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
                   || path.StartsWith("/account", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
        }
    }
}
